_.py` to Scope and specify its `tier2` subparser (with `--candidate` and `--criteria`) plus a `_run_tier2` dispatch branch, since the ACs invoke `tier2` as a CLI subcommand.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.1889,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Scope lists only `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier2.py`, the sample JSON, generated `tier2-*.md`, and the test — no `__main__.py`","`__main__.py` build_parser adds subparsers for `tier0` and `tier1` only; `main()` dispatches only those two and otherwise `return 2`","ACs reference invocations `tier2 --candidate <registry-dir>` and `tier2 --criteria <id>`"],"finding":"The CLI dispatcher `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/__main__.py` — a consumer OUTSIDE the named artifact `tier2.py` — must be updated to expose the `tier2` subcommand, but Scope does not enumerate it. The plan's Approach and Acceptance Criteria depend on `tier2 --candidate <registry-dir>` and `tier2 --criteria <id>` being invocable, yet `build_parser()` registers only `tier0`/`tier1` subparsers and `main()` returns 2 for any other command; without editing this file the `tier2` CLI the ACs check does not exist.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe35a9051b9191671","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope section (file list) / Acceptance Criteria (`tier2 --candidate`, `tier2 --criteria`)","norm_id":"nf9e8d9e86162b5b2","priority":0.8889,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer builds tier2.py to spec but the `tier2` CLI subcommand cannot be run, so the report/ledger ACs cannot be exercised as written"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"List `__main__.py` in Scope and note it gains a `tier2` subparser (mirroring the existing tier0/tier1 pattern: `--candidate`, `--criteria`, `--store`, `--cache-dir`, `--out-dir`) and a `_run_tier2` branch in `main()`.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Specify how Tier-1 is fed the candidate findings given it only scores against STORED verifications — e.g. run the current Pass-2 verifier on the candidate findings to synthesize a baseline, or state the new comparison machinery Tier-2 adds.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2889,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["tier1.replay_review reads `findings = data['findings']` (STORED sidecar findings) and builds `stored_answers` from `f.get('verification')`","tier1.per_question_agreement / distribution_shift zip stored_answers against candidate_answers — there is no path that scores findings lacking a stored verification","A Tier-2 candidate finding is generated fresh in this run, so it carries no `verification` field to serve as the stored baseline"],"finding":"The plan's 'then run Tier 1 on the candidate findings' step is not mechanically achievable with the existing Tier-1 seam: Tier-1 measures agreement/distribution-shift of candidate verifier answers ONLY against STORED per-finding verifications, and freshly-generated Tier-2 candidate findings have no stored verification baseline to compare against.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f70a6afc7add5700b","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → Full mode: 'then run Tier 1 (current questions) on the candidate findings and Tier 0 downstream'","norm_id":"ncc97a347e9e27eb5","priority":0.8889,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Full-mode run over the fixed sample tries to chain new candidate findings into Tier-1 and finds every candidate finding has no stored answer to compare"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"State which criterion families single-criterion mode supports and how each is invoked (single-turn pass1_chunk for 1-TURN prose; agentic pass1_chunk for code-grounded; pass1_container for G3/G4), and correct the 'seam probe_criteria uses' description to the actual finder call seam.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.3,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["`probe_criteria` is a WORKFLOW INPUT consumed by plan_review_assemble_criteria to force a routing allowlist (workflow_ops.py `probe = {..ctx.inputs.get('probe_criteria')..}`), not a per-criterion single-turn calling seam","Container criteria G3/G4 are `CONTAINER_CRITERIA` and run via the dedicated `pass1_container` per-child loop (pass1.py `_run_container`), never a single-turn `pass1_chunk` of one","Code-grounded criteria (A1/E4/G1G2/G6) run agentic (`execution_mode='agentic'`), not single-turn — so 'single-turn chunk of one' and the '≈$0.17 single-turn' cost model do not hold for them"],"finding":"Single-criterion mode is described as 'a single-turn chunk of one (via the same seam probe_criteria uses)', but this mischaracterizes both the seam and the execution mode for whole criterion families.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb4708461b8b41dd1","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → Single-criterion mode; Testing (‘issues exactly one chunk per sampled review’)","norm_id":"n3ba3c7c1eb802894","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["`--criteria G4` (a container criterion) or `--criteria G6` (agentic) selected: the 'single-turn chunk of one' mechanism cannot represent how that criterion actually runs in production"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify how single-criterion mode executes an AGENT-tier / code-grounded criterion (e.g. T5c, T10, T11, E4, G1G2): state whether it runs agentically (multi-turn, tool-using) or is forced single-turn, and correct the cost model + the 'single-turn criterion' AC so the per-criterion cost/ledger check is well-defined for both 1-TURN and AGENT criteria.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: '--criteria T5c runs only the named criteria (single-turn chunk of one, via the same seam probe_criteria uses) … cost ≈ N × $0.17' and Context: 'one single-turn call ≈ $0.17 at 30k Opus input'","registry.py: `AGENT_TIER = {\"G1G2\",\"E4\",\"A1\",\"G6\",\"T5c\",\"T10\",\"T11\",\"G3\",\"G4\"}` and `exec_tier` returns 'AGENT' for T5c","registry.chunk_by_facet docstring: 'Single-turn / 2-step tier only — AGENT criteria run one per call (not chunked).'; pass1.run_pass1 dispatches agent criteria with `agentic=True` (a tool-using, multi-turn call)","workflow_ops.assemble (probe branch) and production_batch_runner._project_criteria only FILTER the included criterion set; the single-turn-vs-agent call mode is decided by registry.exec_tier, not by probe_criteria — so 'the same seam probe_criteria uses' does not by itself yield a single-turn call for an AGENT criterion"],"finding":"Single-criterion mode is specified as a 'single-turn chunk of one' (~one $0.17 call), but its worked example `--criteria T5c` names an AGENT-tier code-grounded criterion that the executor routes to the AGENTIC (multi-turn, tool-using) path, not a single-turn chunk — the execution protocol for a named criterion is under-specified/contradictory.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f47643f5612e131a7","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → 'Single-criterion mode' bullet; Acceptance Criteria line 3 ('single-turn criterion')","norm_id":"nfce0fb757fecdb59","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Author runs `tier2 --criteria T5c`; the criterion executes agentically (several tool calls per sampled review), so the per-sample cost and call count are not the single $0.17 the cost model and AC assume","AC line 3 ('costs ≤ N × $0.25 in the ledger for a single-turn criterion') is unverifiable for the example criterion because T5c is not single-turn"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Split the single-criterion cost/AC by exec tier: for a 1-TURN criterion assert ≤ N × $0.25; for an AGENT criterion (registry.exec_tier == 'AGENT') run the agentic finder path and use an agent-tier per-sample budget (from coverage.usage.per_criterion for that AGENT criterion), and reword the AC to name the tier it applies to.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"broken_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"high","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add an acceptance criterion (or fold into AC3/AC4) that verifies the one-time regver-baseline run is recorded in the ledger and used as the comparison baseline.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'The baseline for a criterion whose stored findings were produced under a different `regver` is a one-time baseline run recorded in the ledger'","No AC references regver, baseline runs, or the ledger baseline record"],"finding":"The Approach describes a one-time baseline run 'recorded in the ledger' for criteria whose stored findings used a different regver, but no acceptance criterion covers verifying that baseline-ledger record, leaving described work uncovered.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe4b0b92f4cd5574e","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach (baseline paragraph) vs Acceptance Criteria","norm_id":"n7e4ad6447878c142","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A criterion edit whose baseline needs re-establishment ships without any check that the baseline run was recorded correctly"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Define the baseline ledger entry lifecycle: what key it is stored under (regver + sample identity), how a comparison selects the right one, and when a baseline is invalidated/retired (e.g., when the fixed sample or prompt changes).","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.28,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'The baseline for a criterion whose stored findings were produced under a different regver is a one-time baseline run recorded in the ledger; otherwise the stored findings are the baseline.'","ABSENCE: no owner, no retirement/cleanup path, and no staleness/invalidation rule for baseline ledger entries is described (e.g., what invalidates a recorded baseline when the fixed sample or prompt changes)."],"finding":"The plan introduces a baseline ledger entry keyed by regver ('a one-time baseline run recorded in the ledger') as shared, accumulating state, but does not define its retirement/cleanup path or staleness rules — as criteria and regvers churn, baseline entries accumulate and it is unspecified which baseline a comparison consumes when multiple regvers exist or when the fixed sample itself changes.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd34aa7948cb7fae5","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → 'The baseline for a criterion whose stored findings were produced under a different regver is a one-time baseline run recorded in the ledger'","norm_id":"n20b6189503b187a1","priority":0.67,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The fixed sample file is regenerated but old regver baselines remain in the ledger, so a comparison silently uses a baseline computed over a different sample set, yielding wrong gained/lost tables.","Baseline entries accumulate across many regvers with no cleanup, and it is ambiguous which entry a given comparison selects."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Define the single-criterion baseline for a sampled review with zero stored findings for that criterion (e.g. treat as an empty baseline so any new finding is 'gained', vs. excluding un-triggered reviews) and how it interacts with the regver one-time-baseline branch.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.03,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'compares only that criterion's findings' and 'otherwise the stored findings are the baseline' — no case given for zero stored findings for that criterion on a given sampled review","Many criteria are overlay/triggered (e.g. T5c fires only on trust-boundary-crossing plans), so a fixed ~20-review sample will routinely include reviews where the criterion produced no stored finding — the gained/lost-per-criterion comparison then has an undefined baseline for that review"],"finding":"Single-criterion mode compares 'only that criterion's findings' against a stored baseline but specifies no behavior for a sampled review that has NO stored findings for the criterion under test (criterion not triggered on that plan / empty baseline).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ffeb532da994376e2","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → 'Single-criterion mode' and the baseline/regver bullet","norm_id":"nfedcb1c6aea70483","priority":0.67,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A sampled review never triggered the criterion under test at review time → the harness must still decide whether a newly-produced finding counts as 'gained' vs. an out-of-scope run"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Give AC2 a concrete proving command and name the report artifact path (e.g. `tier2 --candidate <dir>` writes `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/tier2-<candidate>.md`; assert the Jaccard/gained-lost/Tier-1/Tier-0 tables exist with `jq`/grep on that file).","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'produces finding-set Jaccard and gained/lost-per-criterion tables plus downstream Tier-1/Tier-0 metrics; checked by one generated report'","The commissioning live run is a 'full-mode baseline over the fixed sample', not a --candidate run, so no AC or step names the command that emits the candidate report artifact"],"finding":"AC2 ('produces finding-set Jaccard and gained/lost-per-criterion tables plus downstream Tier-1/Tier-0 metrics; checked by one generated report') names no concrete proving command and does not say which invocation produces the report, so done-ness of the candidate path is not verifiable in-session.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa2a81a879729512c","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, AC2","norm_id":"n90f7d3018b35afe3","priority":0.55,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer must confirm AC2 but there is no named command or artifact path (e.g. tier2-*.md) tying the check to a deterministic output"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"State: `tier2 --candidate <registry-dir>` emits `tier2-<candidate>.md`; verify with a grep/jq assertion on the four required table sections; note whether the commissioning full-mode baseline run also exercises the candidate report path or defer it explicitly.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a doc/ADR (or an update to the plan-review-gate docs) describing the tier2 CLI modes, the fixed-sample contract, and the regver-baseline workflow.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["T7","T5e"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7929,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["New commands `tier2 --candidate <registry-dir>` and `tier2 --criteria T5c` introduced","Scope lists only tier2.py, sample.json, tier2-*.md, and the test file — no doc/ADR for the new CLI/stage"],"finding":"The plan adds a new CLI seam (`tier2 --candidate` / `tier2 --criteria`) and a new eval pipeline stage but names no doc/ADR/AGENTS.md update for the new subcommand and its modes, only auto-generated experiment artifacts.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff906f753e81f7573","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope / Approach (new tier2.py CLI)","norm_id":"n086ad6547b948295","priority":0.1571,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future operator running per-criterion Tier-2 evals has no documented reference for full vs single-criterion mode, the fixed-sample contract, or the regver-baseline workflow"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify error handling for the Bedrock call path: retry/backoff on transient failures, durable per-review/per-criterion partial results so a failed full-mode run can resume without re-spending, and a per-call failure log/metric.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'run the candidate registry/prompts through ProductionBatchRunner/run_pass1 with the frontier class pinned to Bedrock Opus'","'Live (commissioning, ≤$60): one full-mode baseline over the fixed sample.'","ABSENCE: no retry/backoff/circuit-breaker, no resume-from-partial, and no failure instrumentation is described for the Bedrock call path across ~240 finder calls."],"finding":"The harness makes many external Bedrock Opus calls (~20 reviews × ~12 criteria in full mode, up to a $60 live run) but the plan states no error handling, retry/backoff, or resumability for a failed/throttled call — a failure partway through a full-mode run leaves the spend consumed with no durable partial state to resume from, and no metric/log to see which criterion/review failed.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff3bf22b30166c0a9","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → 'Full mode' and Testing → 'Live (commissioning, ≤$60)'","norm_id":"n3d644c30d9e0c7e7","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Bedrock throttles or errors on review 15 of 20 during the $60 baseline run: the run aborts, the spend is lost, and there is no durable checkpoint to resume from, forcing a full re-run.","An operator cannot tell which review/criterion failed because no per-call failure metric/log is specified."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"f3d136f766a0b0ff","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["fac140b6f88006f5",3476],"description_boxes":["7879981d4f226a8f",0],"file_impact":["d127a07c00517b93",4],"ti